{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00443",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.55,
      "end_seconds": 3.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Afternoon. Take the chair by the desk."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.52,
      "end_seconds": 5.22,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hello."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 5.87,
      "end_seconds": 10.98,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Right, doctor, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.7,
      "end_seconds": 15.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Go ahead, tell me what's happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.26,
      "end_seconds": 30.13,
      "duration_seconds": 13.87,
      "text": "I've been getting out of puff on the stairs. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.05,
      "end_seconds": 34.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "How long are we talking about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.26,
      "end_seconds": 51.77,
      "duration_seconds": 16.51,
      "text": "I've had it for about a week. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.63,
      "end_seconds": 58.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.97,
      "end_seconds": 75.94,
      "duration_seconds": 15.97,
      "text": "A five out of ten, I suppose. It's worse with stairs. It happens a couple of times a week. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.45,
      "end_seconds": 82.94,
      "duration_seconds": 6.49,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 83.04,
      "end_seconds": 89.71,
      "duration_seconds": 6.67,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.22,
      "end_seconds": 92.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.27,
      "end_seconds": 111.81,
      "duration_seconds": 17.54,
      "text": "Oh, as for having put on weight, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. I've been feeling tired too, for about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.38,
      "end_seconds": 117.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.82,
      "end_seconds": 123.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Oh, um, pretty severe, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.05,
      "end_seconds": 124.83,
      "duration_seconds": 0.78,
      "text": "I see."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.15,
      "end_seconds": 137.8,
      "duration_seconds": 9.65,
      "text": "I mean, I did have a dry cough at night at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 138.34,
      "end_seconds": 142.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Yes, that's right, that's how it was."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 152.41,
      "end_seconds": 160.66,
      "duration_seconds": 8.25,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Pressure 110 over 79, saturation 99 percent, pulse 86. Temperature is 36.8 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.1,
      "end_seconds": 163.8,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.78,
      "end_seconds": 169.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Right, if you're comfortable, I'll examine you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.35,
      "end_seconds": 173.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Just relax, I'll be quick."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.6,
      "end_seconds": 193.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal and the chest is clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.56,
      "end_seconds": 197.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Just relax, I'll be quick."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.27,
      "end_seconds": 218.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.39,
      "text": "Your BMI is on the high side and you look a little pale."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.47,
      "end_seconds": 225.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Okay, finished. Any calf swelling or coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.14,
      "end_seconds": 228.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.44,
      "end_seconds": 234.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Any palpitations, chest pain or wheezing at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.92,
      "end_seconds": 237.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "No, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.08,
      "end_seconds": 245.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.19,
      "end_seconds": 247.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.63,
      "end_seconds": 252.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Alright, how about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.59,
      "end_seconds": 258.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "My heart's been fine, as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.72,
      "end_seconds": 261.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "How do you eat, generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.12,
      "end_seconds": 268.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "I skip breakfast most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.22,
      "end_seconds": 272.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "What kind of work do you do?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.65,
      "end_seconds": 278.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "I work on a farm, it's quite physical."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.45,
      "end_seconds": 286.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Before I prescribe anything, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.63,
      "end_seconds": 301.77,
      "duration_seconds": 14.14,
      "text": "Hmm, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.06,
      "end_seconds": 306.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.59,
      "end_seconds": 311.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "My sister has thyroid problems."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.12,
      "end_seconds": 320.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 323.0,
      "end_seconds": 325.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.9,
      "end_seconds": 330.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 331.1,
      "end_seconds": 345.87,
      "duration_seconds": 14.77,
      "text": "She takes iron tablets, once a day. It's Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day, doctor. Yeah, she is on amlodipine, once a day, I give it to her."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.74,
      "end_seconds": 349.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Right, how much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 350.08,
      "end_seconds": 350.99,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "5 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.35,
      "end_seconds": 356.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 357.43,
      "end_seconds": 360.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "I've got low haemoglobin. I have diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.77,
      "end_seconds": 363.47,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Ah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.19,
      "end_seconds": 368.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.86,
      "end_seconds": 369.76,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "And then?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.37,
      "end_seconds": 400.65,
      "duration_seconds": 25.28,
      "text": "Right, so low haemoglobin and diabetes are already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Having listened and examined, I don't have a clear answer today: breathlessness with several possible contributors is possible, and so is anaemia. So, to recap quickly. You've been getting out of puff on the stairs for about a week, and no wheezing or palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 402.7,
      "end_seconds": 404.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "That's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 405.75,
      "end_seconds": 426.52,
      "duration_seconds": 20.77,
      "text": "Let's book an echocardiogram to look into breathlessness. I'll request a chest X-ray, it'll help with breathlessness. A short daily walk, building up slowly, is a sensible start. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. Alright, I'll see you out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 427.35,
      "end_seconds": 430.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "I appreciate it, uh, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 431.41,
      "end_seconds": 432.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Bye for now."
    }
  ]
}